WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Just give us a little glimpse into what some of your other daily health habits look like.

00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,840
Well, I like to eat donuts. And we all.

00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:18,240
So my daily health habits should be much better than they currently are. I'm addicted to

00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:28,000
studying and learning and listening to audiobooks and podcasts like yours. So by probably my biggest

00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,280
daily health habit has to do with just being in prayer and just time, just quiet time.

00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:41,440
That to me is the most important thing because all the stresses that you have in life and being a

00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:50,400
clinician, I am an empath. So I take on all my patient's burdens really easy. And it affects me.

00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:56,960
It could affect me very negatively. So I have to really make time to just purposefully

00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:04,960
give them back to God in prayer. Otherwise, it could just eat at me. So that's probably my most

00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:12,640
important. If I don't do that on a very regular basis, I notice my health slipping. So diet is

00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:22,400
important. I try to eat almost exclusively gluten free, dairy free because of my cancer. I don't

00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:29,920
eat much meat at all for when I first diagnosed with cancer. It's just completely dairy and any

00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:37,120
animal protein free except for some fish. Now I've maybe once or twice a month. I'll eat a little

00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:44,960
chicken. But so diet is my cancer happens to be driven slightly off of animal protein. So I have to

00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:52,320
be careful of that. And then again, the biggest thing is that is tried to give back to God

00:01:52,800 --> 00:02:00,560
the burdens of my patients. And then actively be praying for my patients. It's one of my biggest health

00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,520
benefits. So

